[{"text":"TimedIntegrate[exp, vars] is like Integrate, but stops after the number of seconds specified by the option Timing. Options of Integrate can be given and are passed on.","anchor":"timedintegrate"},{"text":"Overview","anchor":"see-also","section":"See also"},{"text":"This should reach to be done","anchor":"examples","section":"Examples"},{"text":"TimedIntegrate[Log[x^5], {x, 0, 1}, Timing -> 1]","anchor":"cb1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[-5\\]","anchor":"cb1-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"This shouldn’t","anchor":"cb1-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"TimedIntegrate[Log[Cos[x^5]], {x, 0, 1}, Timing -> 10, Integrate -> int]","anchor":"cb2","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\text{int}\\left(\\log \\left(\\cos \\left(x^5\\right)\\right),\\{x,0,1\\},\\text{Assumptions}\\to \\varepsilon >0\\right)\\]","anchor":"cb2-1","section":"Examples"}]